WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.080
It's 8 p.m. on Saturday.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.380
Officers Rainer Fuchs and Alexander Schwarzer
are starting their shift.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:14.099
Their beat is Cologne's so-called party mile,
chasing down speeders - mostly young men with

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:18.680
fast cars who race through the city.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.930
Many street races start like this:
"Waiting at a traffic light they'll look at

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:28.199
each other and say: Hey, check it out - you're
low, big and broad.

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:31.480
But I'm even lower and bigger and have way
more under the hood.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.500
So let's go!"

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.760
After just 10 minutes, they spot something.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.829
"That one there"
"The Audi."

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:44.560
"Slow down a bit.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.719
Otherwise you'll give yourself away."

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:54.660
"As you heard just now he was revving his
car pretty loudly."

00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:01.440
"Let's pull him over."

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:11.000
The driver, a young man, fits the street racer
profile, most of whom are male between 18

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.000
and 27.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.689
Street racers tune their cars.

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:15.150
Often without permits.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.060
And many of the changes are illegal.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.110
What's been changed?

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.090
"What it says on the registration."

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.799
"What does it say?"

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:30.030
There are a number of ways to tune a car:
engine, suspension, exhaust.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:32.170
The police inspect the car on site.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:35.540
They know what to look for.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:42.350
"You're allowed 73 according to vehicle registration,
but you're at 80 with this.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.350
That's too much."

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:47.770
"Fact is, his exhaust has been tinkered with.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:49.470
The operating license is expired.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:53.620
And the car's performance has been enhanced,
which has been registered, but the inspection

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.369
authority should have another look."

00:01:55.369 --> 00:01:59.600
The car gets confiscated for the weekend.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.900
On Monday, it will go to inspection for a
technical review.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:08.079
There will likely be a fine or a warning,
but that hardly scares off most racers.

00:02:08.079 --> 00:02:13.050
"It's about showing off, to improve their
standing - their social status."

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:19.989
"They probably think that they're great drivers.

00:02:19.989 --> 00:02:24.700
But unfortunately they're often not.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:31.060
Which is also why we keep seeing these terrible
accidents."

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.870
One fatal incident happened on Cologne's Auenweg.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:39.819
An illegal race resulted in one of the drivers
losing control of the car and slamming into

00:02:39.819 --> 00:02:41.230
a cyclist.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:43.200
She died of her injuries.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.690
The victim was 19 years old.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.700
The driver was convicted of involuntary manslaughter.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:54.970
"In the wake of the accident we learned just
how much street racing has spread into the

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:59.820
city, and how dangerous it is."

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:03.400
Cologne's street racing taskforce was set
up in 2015.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:08.580
Come 11 p.m., it's primetime for them.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:14.530
More alcohol, and more testosterone means
more racers coming their way.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:17.530
And here's another suspect.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:21.209
"Another modified car.

00:03:21.209 --> 00:03:24.230
You can see the upgraded exhaust, different
doors.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.390
The car's moving pretty quickly."

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:31.019
What really stands out though are the struts.

00:03:31.019 --> 00:03:34.470
But the driver refuses to hand over his keys.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:39.489
"You can either follow orders by choice or
by force.

00:03:39.489 --> 00:03:42.890
Then they'll be another car here, and another
- and we'll take your car in the end, believe

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:43.890
me.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.550
I need you car keys, please."

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.480
"No, you're not getting them."

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.500
"Then we'll tow the car."

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:54.379
The taskforce says any car that's been tuned
beyond what's allowed is a potential racer

00:03:54.379 --> 00:03:56.270
and danger to others.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:04:00.130
Which is why night after night, the officers'
search continues.

